<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4. </span>Entity-conditional hierarchical encoding at <math id="S4.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L{=}6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L{=}6</annotation></semantics></math>. Hier. scope is the set of positions whose identifier is conditioned on the predicted entity; <math id="S4.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{HR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{HR}</annotation></semantics></math> is the change in Order HR<math id="S4.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="@350" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>350</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">@350</annotation></semantics></math> against the matched non-hierarchical baseline.</figcaption>
